                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp",
                    "line": 341,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This code looks like it's trying to map a PCIeSlot to be equivalent to a PCIeDevice.  That's not correct.  We either have\n\nthe old way:\nItem.Board -> connected_to -> Item.PcieSlot -> connected_to -> Item.Board\n// IE, the board has a slot that has another board plugged into it\n\n\nOr the new way:\nItem.Board -> Connected_to -> Item.Board\n\nIe, the board has another board plugged into it.\n\n\nWhat this patchset looks like it's doing is extracting all the device inventory items off of the PCIeSlot itself.  I'm not sure where that's implemented in a backend, but it's almost certainly incorrect."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/pcie.hpp",
                    "line": 341,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "I changed to use a new association `{connecting/connected_to}` between PCIeDevice & cpu.\n```\nPCIeDevice -> connected_to -> Cpu\n```"
                }
            ],
